The Gaussian Mixture Model processes the scaled feature matrix:

python
X_scaled
which contains standardized versions of:

SW_P_PSEUDO_N — proton density
SW_P_PSEUDO_V — proton velocity
It estimates clusters or regimes in this two-dimensional feature space.

Each learned component represents a candidate solar-wind state or plasma regime.

Main processing flow
The engine works like this:

Read raw SWAPI CSV
    Using Pandas
Clean rows
    Drop missing density or velocity values
Extract feature matrix
    Density and velocity into NumPy array X
Standardize features
    Using StandardScaler
Fit Gaussian Mixture Model
    Learn fuzzy plasma-regime boundaries
Assign state labels
    Using fit_predict()
Evaluate number of states
    Using BIC, AIC, and KMeans inertia
Summarize states
    Using Pandas groupby
Visualize results
    Using Matplotlib

