Critical failure points
utliers and extreme values
The density distribution includes a high maximum:

Metric	Density
Mean	6.97
Std. dev.	14.47
Max	566.04
This indicates strong outliers or rare high-density events.

Outliers can dominate clustering and create states that represent artifacts rather than meaningful regimes.

Failure modes:
One small state becomes an “outlier bucket”
Normal regimes are distorted
GMM covariance estimates become unstable
High-density events are over- or under-emphasized

Mitigation:
Use physical plausibility checks
Flag extreme density and velocity values
Compare models with and without outliers
Consider log-transforming density before scaling
Review high-density state manually